A||N||12||Predator||Has anybody Intercooled their Turbo setup?||||5||
Z||000000||Predator||03-28-2001||06:23 PM||||I have searched and found a lot of posts about intercooling the Turbo on a Fiero, but I have yet to find someone who has actually done it. I want to intercool mine, and I beleave it can be done, but it would be nice to hear from someone who already has so I will know what to look out for. If you have can you please show some pictures of where you put it, and how you did the plumbing. This information would be most appreciated.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||03-28-2001||08:47 PM||||I've been thinking about putting one where the battery normally goes (and moving battery to the front).<BR>For an air/air intercooler, use something like the IRM rocker panels which have a non-functional scoop on the right side. Make the scoop functional by cutting out holes behind it in the panel. Do some cutting and welding on the body so that the air going into that scoop can come into the engine compartment under the original battery tray, and put a custom intercooler between that and the right deck vent. You may need to include an electric fan triggered by inlet air temp to pull air up through the intercooler. Have you read my post about using the Fiero A/C to intercool a turbo? that system could be used to augment the air/air setup I just described.<P>implementing a air/water intercooler should be significantly simpler: Just find a place to put the cooler, a place to put the pump, run the hoses, add an appropriate radiator in front, and put louvres in the hood.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||BBBAD GT||03-29-2001||02:32 PM||||Here is some good reading: <A HREF="http://www.merkurencyclopedia.com/Motor/water_ic_ed.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.merkurencyclopedia.com/Motor/water_ic_ed.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.merkurencyclopedia.com/Motor/intercooler.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.merkurencyclopedia.com/Motor/intercooler.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.merkurxr4ti.com/thesystem.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.merkurxr4ti.com/thesystem.html</A> <P>There was an excellent site I can't seem to find now, it delt with the AC as IC issues and all sorts of theories.  I'll post it if I find it.<P>BTW, what kind of HP did your turbo motor make?<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">      <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT (sold)</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Predator||03-29-2001||03:06 PM||||Thanks for the reply guys. I have been thinking of putting the intercooler under the vent. It will fit barely. It would take some custom plumbing to make it all come together. I may add the Mustang scoop to give the engine more room to let off heat since I will be using one of the vents. I kind of worry about the view being blocked. It is hard to see now to backup, and a scoop will just make it harder. The hp was a little disapointing 165 hp 207 lbs. The car was running lean, and I found where the distributer cap was barely on so that could have caused the numbers to be low. After I thightened the cap down she ran a lot better. I haven't had it redyno'ed yet. My wife is kind of on my back for the amount of money I have spent already on the car. I sent Ed at Performance an email on the Dyno results, and I sent one to Kevin at Design One about the lean condition. I haven't heard back from either yet. I can't even get in it hard until I am sure the lean condition is fixed. After about 3800 RPM's it starts leaning out so the first Dyno run really didn't show what the car can do. Anyway I will post the results when I get it Dyno'ed again. Thanks for the ideas on the intercooler guys. I will check them out. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
