Z||000006||rogergarrison||03-29-2001||08:49 PM||||ive thought about both ways. air to air would be pretty ez on my car. Ferrari body has an available scoop behind the door. also though about using a heater core just inside it by the battery. Just filling it with some liquid supercool and a ww pump to circulate it in a loop. I already have one side hooked up to air cleaner for ram air.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula 18||03-30-2001||12:00 AM||||Why not a WATER INJECTION setup. You could put the tank where the batter sits now and plumbimg water lines is a lot EZer that tryin to plumb all that compressed air around. You have to think about flow and PSi loss after the compresser if you have to move all that sir around corners. With a water injection setup you wouldn't have to change the plumbing just add a tank, psi selonoid,a few lines, and a nozle. It could all be done for under a $100 dollars and is just as effective as a Icebox. <P>Check it out:  <A HREF="http://home.ccci.org/Key_Information/2ndWaterInjection.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.ccci.org/Key_Information/2ndWaterInjection.htm</A> <P>Just my 2 cents. <BR>Brian ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bill H||03-30-2001||08:00 AM|||| Do any of you know if you can use sprint manifolds with the design one system?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Predator||03-30-2001||10:36 AM||||I am not sure what sprint manifolds are, but the crossover pipe will bolt to manifolds that are in the stock position. If they will bolt to your stock cross over pipe then they will bolt to the Design One Systems X- pipe. If you ordered it from Design One and told them what manifolds you were using I am sure they can make a crossover pipe that would work. Kevin at Design One is real easy to talk to if you have any questions. <A HREF="http://www.Design1Systems.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.Design1Systems.com</A>   <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
